; Error cases of a double-quoted token in a value expression; the amount and
; string readings are in expr-quoted-token.test.  When amount_t::parse
; rejects the quoted text with an error, the token falls back to the string
; reading, so the error reported is the string reader's.

; With a space on each side the minus sign is the subtraction operator.
test eval '"ab" - 1' -> 1
__ERROR__
While evaluating value expression:
  ("ab" - 1)
  ^^^^^^^^^^
While subtracting 1 from ab:
Error: Cannot subtract an amount from a string
end test

; amount_t::parse throws "Quoted commodity symbol lacks closing quote" here;
; the string reader's diagnostic is the one reported.
test eval '"ab\"' -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing value expression:
  "ab\"

Error: Missing '"'
end test
